From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LuneOS <dev@luneos.org>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 19:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] vpn-provider: skip connections with no object path in
 GetConnections

net.connman.vpn.Manager.GetConnections() crashes connman-vpnd the moment
anything calls it, on a completely stock install with zero VPN profiles
ever configured (/var/lib/connman-vpn empty). append_connection_structs()
iterates provider_hash and skips entries with no identifier, but not
entries with no path:

    DBG("path %s", provider->path);          -> logs "path (null)"
    if (!provider->identifier)
            continue;
    ...
    dbus_message_iter_append_basic(&entry, DBUS_TYPE_OBJECT_PATH,
                    &provider->path);

Passing a NULL object-path string to dbus_message_iter_append_basic()
trips libdbus's own _dbus_check_is_valid_path() assertion and the process
aborts (SIGABRT), tearing down every VPN connection along with it - not a
graceful per-call failure.

There is at least one provider_hash entry with an identifier but no path
by the time GetConnections() first runs, independent of any provider a
caller has configured. Skip it the same way a missing identifier already
is, rather than handing libdbus a NULL.

Found via connman_vpn_client.c's connman_vpn_client_create() eagerly
calling GetConnections() as soon as connman-vpnd appears on the bus -
apparently the first thing on a stock LuneOS image to ever make that
call, which is why this had gone unnoticed.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: LuneOS <dev@luneos.org>
---
 vpn/vpn-provider.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/vpn/vpn-provider.c b/vpn/vpn-provider.c
--- a/vpn/vpn-provider.c
+++ b/vpn/vpn-provider.c
@@ -2709,7 +2709,7 @@ static void append_connection_structs(DBusMessageIter *iter, void *user_data)
 
 		DBG("path %s", provider->path);
 
-		if (!provider->identifier)
+		if (!provider->identifier || !provider->path)
 			continue;
 
 		dbus_message_iter_open_container(iter, DBUS_TYPE_STRUCT,
-- 
2.43.0
